1
00:00:13,399 --> 00:00:48,089
来证明任何 p^2 阶群都是……交换群。此前我们已知任何 p 阶群 G 都是循环群，因此通过将循环群的生成元映到1，必同构于群 Z/pZ。
to prove that any group of order p^2 was... abelian. Now, we already knew that any G of order p is cyclic, so therefore isomorphic to the group Z/pZ by sending a generator of the cyclic group to 1.

2
00:00:48,089 --> 00:01:07,550
今天我们要开始发展一些方法来分析 G：若 G 的阶是 pq 或 p^3，即稍复杂的素数乘积，情况又如何？
And we're going to start to develop methods that allow us to analyze G. What about G of order pq, or p^3, slightly more complicated products of primes?

3
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:22,360
我们需要……我们知道这些阶确实存在非交换群：至少对于6 阶，我们有 6 阶群 S_3；上次我还给过大家一个 p^3 阶非交换群的例子，
So we're going to need... We know non-abelian groups of these orders: at least of order 6, we have S_3 of order 6; and last time I gave you an example of a non-abelian group of order p^3,

4
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:30,875
即在 p 元域上取特定矩阵构成的群。因此这些阶存在非常有趣的群，我们希望对它们进行分类。
where you took these matrices over the field of p elements. So there are interesting groups of these orders, and we might want to classify them.

5
00:01:30,875 --> 00:01:36,575
为此，我们需要深入有限群内部发展更多的理论工具。
And to do that, we're going to need to develop a little bit more machinery internal to finite groups.

6
00:01:36,575 --> 00:01:58,893
现在让我们继续探讨这个定理：我断言，一旦我们知道任何p^2 阶群都是交换群，那么它只有两种可能，在同构意义下恰好只有两种群。也就是说，任何 p^2 阶群都必同构于这两个群之一。
Now let's proceed with this theorem a little bit: I claim that once we know that any group of order p^2 is abelian, there are only two possibilities for it, only two such groups up to isomorphism. Namely, any group of order p^2 is going to be isomorphic to one of two groups.

7
00:01:58,893 --> 00:02:21,516
（任何 p 阶群都同构于该群，所以在同构意义下只有一种 p 阶群。）因此对于 p^2 阶群有两种可能：第一种情形是群中存在一个p^2 阶元素 g ∈ G。
(Any group of order p is isomorphic to this group, so there's only one group up to isomorphism of order p.) So for a group of order p^2, there are two possibilities. The first case is that there is an element g in G of order p^2.

8
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:31,413
我是说，p^2 阶群中元素的可能阶只能是 1、p 和 p^2，仅此而已，因为元素的阶必须整除群的阶。
I mean, the possible orders for an element in a group of order p^2 are 1, p, and p^2. Okay, that's it, because the order has to divide the order of the group.

9
00:02:31,413 --> 00:02:59,179
如果存在 p^2 阶元素，那么 G 同构于 Z/p^2Z，建立该同构的映射是将g 映为 1 mod p^2，并将 g^a 映为 a mod p^2。这是一个一一满射，是群同构。
If there's an element of order p^2, then G is isomorphic to Z/p^2Z by the isomorphism that takes g to 1 mod p^2, and that takes g^a to a mod p^2. That's a 1-1 onto map, which is an isomorphism of groups.

10
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:07,593
因此如果存在 p^2 阶元素，它就是一个循环群，同构于这个循环群。
So if you have an element of order p^2, it's a cyclic group, and is isomorphic to this cyclic group.

11
00:03:07,593 --> 00:03:31,180
第二种可能是群中没有 p^2 阶元素，于是每个非单位元 g ≠ e 的阶都为p，对吧？
The second possibility is there is no element of order p^2, so every g not equal to the identity has order p, correct?

12
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:58,574
此时域 Z/pZ 作用在群 G 上：域中的标量 a 与群中的元素 g 的作用定义为g^a。
Then the field Z/pZ acts on the group G by—well, I could say a in this field times an element g in the group is g^a.

13
00:03:59,071 --> 00:04:08,961
这是合理的，因为若在此乘以 p（在域中为 0），对应群中的 g^p 恰好就是单位元。
And that makes sense, because if I multiply by p here, which is zero in this field, g^p is the identity element.

14
00:04:08,961 --> 00:04:16,686
所以必须理解 0 * g 就是群中的单位元 e。
So you have to understand that 0 * g is e, the identity element in the group.

15
00:04:16,686 --> 00:04:30,352
实际上，若将这个没有 p^2 阶元素的群看作加法群会更好，因而 g^a 写成加号形式：不再是乘法 g * h，而是看作 g + h。
In fact, it's better if you think of this group which has no element of order p^2 additively, and therefore g^a—namely with a plus sign: instead of multiplying elements g * h, you think of it as g + h.

16
00:04:30,352 --> 00:04:36,736
这是合理的，因为 G 是交换群，所以g + h 等于 h + g。
That makes sense because G is abelian, so we can think of g + h is the same thing as h + g.

17
00:04:36,736 --> 00:04:56,197
因此这只是 g + g + ... + g（共 a 次），而单位元则可看作加法群中的零元。
So this would just be g + g + g + g, a times, and this would just be the identity element, we could think of as zero in the additive group.

18
00:04:56,197 --> 00:05:28,145
因此在此情形下，我们得到群 G 实际上是该域上的一个向量空间：即它是一个交换群，伴随着域在该群上的作用——这就是域在群上的数乘运算。
And consequently, what we get in this case is that the group G is actually a vector space over this field: namely, it's an abelian group together with an operation of a field on the group—here is scalar multiplication of the field on the group.

19
00:05:28,145 --> 00:05:35,280
因此它是 Z/pZ 上的向量空间。其阶数为 p^2，因此维数为2。
And consequently it's a vector space over Z/pZ. It has order p^2, so it has dimension 2.

20
00:05:37,831 --> 00:05:47,164
所以作为交换群，G 同构于 (Z/pZ)^2，因为那是 p 元域上的二维向量空间。
So as an abelian group, G is isomorphic to (Z/pZ)^2, because that's the two-dimensional vector space over the field of p elements.

21
00:05:47,164 --> 00:05:52,433
每个二维向量空间在选定基后都同构于它。
Every two-dimensional vector space is isomorphic to this one by the choice of a basis.

22
00:05:52,433 --> 00:06:13,462
因此要给出具体的同构，你只需在 G 中找到两个不同元素 g_1 与 g_2，使其构成 Z/pZ 上向量空间的基，然后将 g_1^{a_1}g_2^{a_2} 映为坐标 (a_1, a_2)。
So to make this specific isomorphism, you'd have to find two different elements g_1 and g_2 in G that gave a basis for it as a vector space over Z/pZ, and you take g_1^{a_1} g_2^{a_2} to the coordinates (a_1, a_2).

23
00:06:13,462 --> 00:06:22,223
所以若每个元素的阶都是 p，域就会作用在群上，使群成为二维向量空间，从而得到该群。
So if every element has order p, then you have an action of the field on the group, turning the group into a two-dimensional vector space, and you get this.

24
00:06:22,223 --> 00:06:30,639
而该群不同构于前一个群，因为前一个群包含p^2 阶元素，而在这个群中所有非单位元的阶都是 p。
And that group is not isomorphic to this group, because this group has elements of order p^2, whereas in this group everything has order p.

25
00:06:30,639 --> 00:06:44,160
前一个群不是 p 元域上的向量空间，因为在p 元域上的向量空间中，p 乘以任何元素都是零；而这里存在必须乘以 p^2 才能得到零的元素。
This is not a vector space over the field of p elements, because in a vector space over the field of p elements, p * anything is zero, whereas here you have things where you have to multiply by p^2 till you get zero.

26
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:49,373
顺便说一句，这给出了一般群的一种极有趣的构造。
This by the way gives a very interesting construction of a group in general.

27
00:06:49,373 --> 00:07:06,587
一般地，若 n >= 1，群 G = (Z/pZ)^n 是 Z/pZ 上的 n 维向量空间。
In general, if n >= 1, we have the group G which is (Z/pZ)^n, an n-dimensional vector space over Z/pZ.

28
00:07:06,587 --> 00:07:20,868
它的阶为 p^n，其中每个非单位元的阶都是 p，正如本例一样。
This has order p^n, every element not equal to the identity has order p, just like in this case.

29
00:07:20,868 --> 00:07:35,220
这是一个如此优良的群，以至于它拥有专有名称，就像循环群有专有名称一样：这被称为初等交换群，初等交换 p-群。
And that's such a nice group that it has a name for it, just like the cyclic group has a name for it: this is called an elementary abelian group, elementary abelian p-group.

30
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:46,356
它在某种意义上是与循环群截然相反的一类交换 p-群，因为其中元素的阶尽可能小（均为 p）；相对应的另一极端则是p^n 阶循环群。
It's sort of the opposite kind of abelian p-group than a cyclic group, in that the elements have as small order as possible, p; whereas the contrast in this case would be a cyclic group of order p^n.

31
00:07:46,356 --> 00:07:52,911
而在 p^2 阶的情形下，只有两种可能：循环群，或者这种初等交换群。
And in order p^2, there are only two possibilities: cyclic, or this.

32
00:07:52,911 --> 00:08:06,640
好，现在讨论更复杂的阶，我们必须发展普遍的定理。此前凭初等方法我们能徒手解决 p 阶和 p^2 阶群；现在我们必须建立一般性定理。
Okay, now to go on to groups of more complicated order, we have to actually develop general theorems. We were able to do groups of order p and p^2 with our bare hands; now we have to develop some general theorems.

33
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:14,203
我们即将发展的普遍定理是在 19 世纪末由一位挪威数学家发现的，他的名字是西罗（Sylow）。
And the general theorems we're going to develop were discovered at the end of the 19th century by a Norwegian mathematician whose name is Sylow.

34
00:08:14,203 --> 00:08:25,374
我们现在要证明，或者说开始证明著名的西罗定理。
And we're going to prove now, or start the proof of what are called the Sylow theorems today.

35
00:08:25,374 --> 00:08:28,572
今天我大概能讲完证明。
And I will probably get through the proof today.

36
00:08:28,572 --> 00:08:39,906
这是一个非常严密的论证，周三我们将开始将其应用到pq 阶等群的分类上。
It's a serious argument, and we'll start doing applications of the proof to groups of order pq, etc., on Wednesday.

37
00:08:39,906 --> 00:08:50,205
我需要说明，周五我要出差：我得去西海岸为哈佛学院从电影大亨那里筹集难以想象的巨额资金！
I should point out that I'm out of town on Friday: I have to go to the West Coast to raise unimaginably large sums of money from movie moguls for Harvard College!

38
00:08:50,205 --> 00:09:00,000
助教 Peter Green 这周余下时间也不在，因为他要去普林斯顿参加一个关于重大数学问题的会议，他对此做出了基础性贡献。
So, and Peter Green is out the rest of this week too, because he's going down to Princeton to participate in a conference on a major mathematical problem to which he's making fundamental contributions.

39
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:08,248
不过周五你们很幸运，我的同事理查德·泰勒（Richard Taylor）——参与证明费马大定理的核心人物之一、一位极其伟大的数论学家—
But on Friday you're lucky that my colleague Richard Taylor, who is one of the people involved in the proof of Fermat's Last Theorem, a great, great number theorist, is going to come to lecture to you;

40
00:09:08,248 --> 00:09:19,987
—将来给大家代课；然后周一由 Peter 替我代课，以便我从旅途中休整恢复。我将在下周三返回并讨论西罗定理的应用。所以回想……不好意思？
and then Peter will sub for me on Monday, as I'm recovering from my various travels. I'll be back on Wednesday, but I'll talk about applications of this on Wednesday.

41
00:09:19,987 --> 00:09:32,309
请讲？抱歉，在您继续前，我这里可能没太跟上。好的，这只是一个例子，推广了我在 p^2 阶中举的例子。
So recall— Excuse me? Yes? Sorry, before you go on, I might lose the point over here. Okay, this is just an example, so that generalizes the example I did in order p^2.

42
00:09:32,309 --> 00:09:50,269
如果你想知道一种从向量空间走向群的极佳方式：取 p 元域上的 n 维向量空间，这就特别给出了一个交换群，因为向量空间其底层是一个交换群。
If you want to know a nice way of going from vector spaces to groups, taking the vector space of dimension n over the field of p elements gives you in particular an abelian group, because a vector space has underlying it an abelian group.

43
00:09:50,269 --> 00:09:55,953
但这是有限交换群，阶为 p^n——这些坐标共有p^n 种选取方式。
But it's a finite abelian group, it has order p^n—there are p^n choices for these coordinates.

44
00:09:55,953 --> 00:10:04,694
群中每个非零元素的阶都是 p，因为考虑群中的加法，若把任何元素相加p 次，就会回到原点零元。
Every element in the group has order p, because when you think about how you add things in this group, if you add anything to itself p times, you get to the origin.

45
00:10:04,694 --> 00:10:12,060
正因为这是如此优良的例子，我们称其为初等交换 p-群，就像我们对其它群也有特定称呼一样。
And we call this, because it's such a nice example, the elementary abelian p-group, okay, just like we have a name for groups.

46
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:27,160
我们正在建立一个有限群的“动物园”：我们已知有限循环群，刚刚又介绍了初等交换 p-群，接下来我们甚至还会对非交换群命名，正如我们将看到的。
So we're developing a kind of menagerie of finite groups: we already know the finite cyclic groups, I've just told you about the elementary abelian p-groups, and we'll even have names for non-abelian groups, as we'll see.

47
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:38,720
我之前向大家展示过的由矩阵给出的 p^3 阶非交换群，即上三角元素构成的矩阵群，被称为海森堡群（Heisenberg group），
The group that I showed you, which was this non-abelian group of order p^3 given by those matrices, those matrices with entries in the upper triangular, is called a Heisenberg group,

48
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:47,764
因为它是海森堡在实数域上所考虑群的代数类比。我们稍后会回到这点。有限群的传统之一就是给各类群命名。
because it's the analog of a group that Heisenberg considered over the real numbers. We'll come back to that. Part of the lore of finite groups is naming everything.

49
00:10:47,764 --> 00:10:59,680
好，西罗定理：我们必须讨论 G 的共轭作用。大家记得 G通过共轭作用于 G 上。
Okay, the Sylow theorems: we have to discuss the operation of G by conjugation. So remember that G acts on G by conjugation.

50
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:18,623
这里将 G 看作被作用的集合：它将元素 s 映为 g s g^{-1}，其轨道称为元素的共轭类。
So this you think of as the set: namely, it takes an element s to g s g^{-1}, and the orbits are called conjugacy classes of elements.

51
00:11:18,623 --> 00:11:31,920
而稳定子群——这就像 O(s)，元素 s 的共轭类，而稳定子群 G_s被称为 s 的中心化子。
And the stabilizers—this is like O(s), conjugacy class of the element s, and the stabilizer G_s is called the centralizer of s.

52
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:43,514
即满足 g s g^{-1} = s 的 g 的集合，也就是与 s 可交换的元素。我们在讲类方程时已经考察过这种作用。
So that's the set of g such that g s g^{-1} = s, the elements that commute with s. So we've taken a look at this action when we did the class equation.

53
00:11:43,514 --> 00:12:12,113
现在，它不仅作用于 G 的元素，还作用于子集：G 作用在——或者我应该说另一种不同的作用，即通过共轭作用在 G 的所有子群构成的集合上。
Now it doesn't just act on G, it acts on subsets: G acts on the set of—or maybe I should say also, because this is a different action, on the set—let's call it H—of all subgroups of G by conjugation.

54
00:12:12,113 --> 00:12:25,160
因此若我有一个子群 H，想知道 g 对它做什么，g 将其映为子群 g H g^{-1}，这也是一个子群。
So if I have a subgroup H, and I want to know what g does to it, it takes it to the subgroup g H g^{-1}, which is another subgroup.

55
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:46,623
好的。是的，G 的所有子群。G 作用在自身的子群上，未必作用在其它群的子群上。群。
Okay. Yeah, of all subgroups of G. G acts on its own subgroups, it doesn't necessarily act on subgroups of another group.

56
00:12:46,623 --> 00:12:59,483
前面 G 通过共轭作用在自身元素上：将群中任意元素映为另一个共轭元素。但这不仅是将元素映为元素。
So here G is acting on its elements by conjugation: you take an arbitrary element in the group to this element in the group. But this doesn't just take elements to elements.

57
00:12:59,483 --> 00:13:15,121
若考虑共轭的作用，若将其作用于某个子群的全体元素——这包含了所有形式为 g h g^{-1}（其中 h ∈ H）的元素——它是 G 的子集，但事实上它也是一个子群：若将其中两个元素相乘，结果仍在其中。
If you think about what conjugation does, if you apply it to the elements of a subgroup—so this consists of all things of the form g h g^{-1} such that h is in H—it's a subset of G, but in fact it's a subgroup: if you multiply two things here, you stay in it.

58
00:13:15,121 --> 00:13:22,805
因此这给出了从一个子群到另一个子群的方式，这是一个 G-作用：即单位元保持所有子群不变，且满足结合律。
So that gives a way of going from one subgroup to another, and that's a G-action: namely, the identity preserves all subgroups and it's associative.

59
00:13:22,805 --> 00:13:31,865
我们学过 G 作用在集合上的概念：这里它作用在自身元素集合上，而在此处它作用在自身子群的集合上。
So we had the notion of G acting on sets: here it's acting on the set of its own elements, here it's acting on the set of its own subgroups, okay.

60
00:13:31,865 --> 00:13:59,520
好，我们想知道其轨道是什么：H 的轨道就是与 H共轭的子群集合，共轭就是指这种形式。而 H 的稳定子群是使得 g H g^{-1} = H 的 g 的集合。
And we want to know what the orbit is: so the orbit of H is the set of subgroups conjugate to H, conjugate meaning of this form. And the stabilizer of H is the set of g such that g H g^{-1} = H.

61
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:10,663
注意这并不意味着逐个元素相等！并不是每个元素都不变，而是指这两个集合相等。它可以把 H 中的元素互相置换。
Now that doesn't mean element by element! That doesn't mean element by element; it means that this set is equal to this set. It could move the elements of H around.

62
00:14:10,663 --> 00:14:16,033
因此不要把它当成 H 的中心化子——它并不与 H 的每个元素都交换，只是将集合整体映到自身。
So you don't think of that as the centralizer of H—it doesn't centralize everything in H, it just takes the set to itself.

63
00:14:16,033 --> 00:14:26,110
所以这就是群论中所称的 H 的正规化子（normalizer）：N_G(H)。
So this is what's called in group theory the normalizer of H.

64
00:14:26,110 --> 00:14:38,738
关于 H 的正规化子我做两点评注：首先，它是一个子群，因为某对象的稳定子群永远是子群；并且它是一个介于 H 与 G 之间的子群，因为 H 显然能正规化自身。
And I'm going to make two comments about the normalizer of H: so first of all, it's a subgroup, because it's the stabilizer of something—the stabilizer of something is always a subgroup.

65
00:14:38,738 --> 00:15:01,447
此外，它是介于 H 与 G 之间的子群，且 H 在自身的正规化子中是正规的。清楚吗？
And it's a subgroup that sits between H and G, because H has the property that it normalizes itself. Moreover, it's a subgroup that sits between H and G, and H is normal in its own normalizer. Clear?

66
00:15:01,447 --> 00:15:09,415
若忽略 G 的作用，仅考虑正规化子中元素的作用，它们保持 H 不变。
If you forget the fact that you're acting by G, and you're just acting by elements in the normalizer, they preserve H.

67
00:15:09,415 --> 00:15:25,469
而且它是 G 中包含 H 的且使得 H 在其中为正规子群的最大子群。
And it's the largest subgroup of G containing H in which H is normal.

68
00:15:25,469 --> 00:15:33,103
我是说，若 H 是 G 的正规子群，那么在此作用下它的稳定子群就是整个群对吧？
I mean, if H is a normal subgroup of G, its stabilizer is the entire group under this action, right?

69
00:15:33,103 --> 00:15:43,645
这就是在 G 中正规的含义：对所有 g，g H g^{-1} = H。对所有 h ∈ H 当然也成立。
That's what it means to be normal in G: that this subgroup is equal to H for all g. It's certainly equal to H for all h.

70
00:15:43,645 --> 00:15:52,637
所以你可以看能在 H 之外添加哪些在共轭下保持 H 的元素，它是 G 中正规化 H 的最大子群。
So you see what you can add to H that preserves H in this conjugation business, and it's the largest subgroup of G that normalizes H.

71
00:15:52,637 --> 00:15:57,635
我给大家举两个正规化子的例子，这是一个重要概念。
So I'll give you two examples of normalizers, it's an important concept.

72
00:15:57,635 --> 00:16:12,318
在群 S_3 中，如果我们考察子群A_3（交错群），它包含单位元、我们新记号下的置换 (1 2 3) 和置换 (1 3 2)，
In the group S_3, if we took a look at the subgroup A_3, the alternating group, which is the identity, the permutation (1 2 3) in our new notation, and the permutation (1 3 2),

73
00:16:12,318 --> 00:16:31,076
即 3 阶元素与单位元：它是 S_3 的正规子群，是唯一的 3 阶子群，所以该群的正规化子 N_{S_3}(A_3) 等于S_3。
namely the elements of order 3 and the identity: that's a normal subgroup of S_3, it's the only subgroup of order 3, so the normalizer of this group, the normalizer of A_3, is equal to S_3.

74
00:16:31,076 --> 00:16:43,987
然而，如果你改为取 S_3 中由 {e, (1 2)} 构成的 2 阶子群，并问哪些元素正规化它？
However, if you took instead the group {e, (1 2)} of order 2 inside of S_3, and you asked what elements normalize this?

75
00:16:43,987 --> 00:16:51,826
若某个元素正规化它，它必须把该元素映为自身，因为该子群中没有其它 2 阶元素。
Well, if they normalize this, they would have to take this element to itself, because there's no other element of order 2 in the subgroup.

76
00:16:51,826 --> 00:17:05,948
你看，在前一个例子中可以通过置换这两个元素来实现正规化，那是可以的；事实上当你用对换共轭 A_3 时，它置换了这两个 3 阶元素。它并不中心化它，但正规化了它。
You see, here you can normalize this by permuting these two elements, that would be okay; and in fact when you conjugate this group by this element, you'll see it permutes those two elements. It doesn't centralize it, but it normalizes it.

77
00:17:05,948 --> 00:17:11,040
而在这里，如果你有一个 2 阶子群且某个元素正规化它，该元素就必须中心化它。
Here, if you have a group of order 2 and you have something that normalizes that, it has to centralize it.

78
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:21,715
若计算哪些元素与该元素交换，除该子群本身外没有其它元素，因此在这种情形下我们发现H 的正规化子就是 H 本身。
And if you calculate what elements commute with this element, there are no other elements but this subgroup, and so in this case one finds the normalizer of H is just H.

79
00:17:21,715 --> 00:17:30,440
所以这是两个极端：要么没有任何其它元素保持该子群，要么是整个群；或者介于两者之间。
So those are the two extremes: you can have nothing else preserving the subgroup, or you can have the entire group, or you can have things in between.

80
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:56,378
如果你想要一个介于两者之间的例子——这同样是一个重要的特殊例子——如果你在 G = GL_2(F)（F 为任意域）中取由形如 [1 b; 0 1] 的 2x2 矩阵构成的子群 H，
If you want an example of something in between—and this is also an important special example—if you take the subgroup H inside of 2x2 matrices that looks like [1 b; 0 1] inside of G = GL_2 over a field,

81
00:17:56,378 --> 00:18:12,790
你会发现 H 的正规化子是由形如 [a b; 0 d] 的矩阵构成的集合（上三角可逆矩阵），像这样。
any field, you'll find that the normalizer of H is the set of matrices that look like this.

82
00:18:12,790 --> 00:18:17,674
这里正规化子比 H 大，但并不是整个 G。
So there's a case where the normalizer is larger, but is not all of G.

83
00:18:17,674 --> 00:18:26,307
好，在陈述西罗定理时，这种语言非常关键，即引入 G 通过共轭作用在其子群集合上的概念。
Okay, so this language is important when you state the Sylow theorems, to have a notion of G acting on its set of subgroups by conjugation.

84
00:18:26,307 --> 00:18:45,089
我们此前已经看到，与给定子群共轭的子群集合在群作用于集合的概念中非常重要，因为若 G 作用在集合上，且我们知道 s 的稳定子群，
We've already seen the set of subgroups conjugate to a given one is important in the notion of group actions on a set, because if G acts on a set and we know the stabilizer of s, that is conjugate to the stabilizer.

85
00:18:45,089 --> 00:18:58,839
它共轭于……抱歉，若传递地作用在 S 上，那么 s 的稳定子群就与另一点的稳定子群共轭，不同的稳定子群构成了一类共轭子群。
.. sorry, acts transitively on S, then the stabilizer of s is conjugate to the stabilizer of another point, and the different stabilizers form a conjugacy class of subgroups.

86
00:18:58,839 --> 00:19:04,982
所以我们之前已经见过这类轨道，但我们需要给稳定子群一个专有名称。
So we've already seen these kinds of orbits already, but we have to have a name for the notion of the stabilizer.

87
00:19:04,982 --> 00:19:14,959
正如我所说，请记住它不必逐点保持 H 的元素不变，它只是将这个集合整体映为自身。
As I say, remember that it does not preserve the points of H pointwise; it just takes this set into this set.

88
00:19:14,959 --> 00:19:27,360
好，现在我们来陈述西罗定理。我需要一块黑板来写它。
Okay, now let's state the Sylow theorems. I need a blackboard for that.

89
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:43,919
它们通常被分为三个部分，尽管西罗当初发现它们时有些混杂在一起。
So they're generally broken up into three parts, although when Sylow discovered them, they were kind of a mishmash.

90
00:19:43,919 --> 00:20:38,896
定理：设 G 为有限群，阶为 |G| = p^m * n，即素数 p 的某次幂乘上一个数，其中 n 与p 互素，使得 p^m 是整除群阶的 p 的最高次幂。好，那么：(1) 存在 G 的一个阶为 p^m 的子群 H。
Theorem: Assume G is a finite group of order N, which is factored as p^m * n, some power of a prime p times a number where n is prime to p, so that this is the highest power of p that divides the order of the group. Okay, then: (1) There is a subgroup H of G of order p^m.

91
00:20:38,896 --> 00:20:53,618
即该阶整除群阶，是子群的可能阶；事实上你总能找到一个阶为整除群阶的 p 的最高次幂的子群。好。(2) 该子群——顺便说一句，
Namely, we have a possible order for a subgroup because this divides the order of the group; in fact, you can always find a subgroup which has order the highest power of p dividing the order of the group.

92
00:20:53,618 --> 00:21:15,188
这些 p^m 阶子群被称为西罗 p-子群（Sylow p-subgroups）；若明确讨论哪个素数有时可省略 p，统称西罗子群。
Okay. Two: this subgroup—these subgroups by the way, of order p^m, are called Sylow p-subgroups; sometimes you omit the p if you know what prime you're talking about, just a Sylow subgroup.

93
00:21:15,188 --> 00:21:50,304
(2)若 K 为任意 p^a 阶子群（已知 a <= m，因为子群的阶必须整除群的阶）——那么 K 必包含在上面找到的西罗 p-子群 H 的某个共轭子群中。
Two: If K is a subgroup of order p^a for any a—we know a <= m because the order of a subgroup has to divide the order of a group—then K is contained in a conjugate of H, the Sylow p-subgroup that we found up there.

94
00:21:50,304 --> 00:22:17,127
因此作为 (2) 的特例，特别地，任何两个西罗 p-子群 H 与 H' 都是共轭的。
So as a particular case of (2), in particular any two Sylow p-subgroups H and H' are conjugate.

95
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:28,259
因为取 K 的阶为 p^m 的情形（即 K 也是西罗 p-子群），定理说 K 包含在 H 的某个共轭子群中。
Because take the case where K has order p^m, so is a Sylow p-subgroup: then this says that K is contained in a conjugate of H.

96
00:22:28,259 --> 00:22:37,448
而 H 的共轭子群具有相同的阶，若两个同阶群其中一个包含在另一个之中，它们必然相等！所以这就表明 K 是 H 的共轭子群。
Well, the conjugates of H have the same order, and if you have two groups of the same order, one contained in the other, they're equal! So that would say that K is a conjugate of H.

97
00:22:37,448 --> 00:22:53,939
因此存在该阶的子群，且任意两个都共轭；反之，H 的任何共轭子群阶相同，也是西罗 p-子群。所以西罗 p-子群恰好构成单个共轭类。
So there are subgroups of this order, any two of them are conjugate; conversely, any conjugate of H is a Sylow p-subgroup because it has the same order. So the Sylow p-subgroups form a single conjugacy class.

98
00:22:53,939 --> 00:23:10,618
这是非常重要的结论，结论不能更优美了！最后，西罗定理的第三部分给出了该共轭类中究竟有多少个西罗 p-子群的估计。
That's an important thing to know, you can't have any better than that! And finally, the third part of the Sylow theorem gives you an estimate of how many Sylow p- subgroups are in that conjugacy class.

99
00:23:10,618 --> 00:23:31,293
(3)数目——我们给这个数目起个记号，我本来想用 s 表示 Sylow，但我最好用别的记号——
(3) The number—let's give that number a name, I was going to call it s for Sylow, but I better use something else—the number, ell,

100
00:23:31,293 --> 00:24:13,930
G 中这单个共轭类内西罗 p-子群的数目 ell，整除剩余的那个数 n——抱歉，整除 n——并且满足 ell ≡ 1 (mod p)，即除以 p 余 1。
of Sylow p-subgroups of G in this single conjugacy divides n, the number that's left over—I'm sorry, divides n—and satisfies ell congruent to 1 mod p, leaves a remainder of 1 after dividing by p.

101
00:24:13,930 --> 00:24:27,503
因此对西罗 p-子群的数目有限制：总是存在西罗 p-子群，任意两个西罗 p-子群都共轭。首先，哪怕仅这一定理的第一部分就极其非凡，绝对非同寻常！
So there's a restriction on the number of Sylow p-subgroups: there is always a Sylow p-subgroup, any two of them are... First of all, even the first part of this theorem is remarkable, it's absolutely remarkable!

102
00:24:27,503 --> 00:25:05,399
若考察 12 阶群，一般阶的子群未必存在，所以我们先作此评注，以便在证明前领会其精妙：注意，若 d 整除群 G 的阶 |G|，G 中未必存在 d 阶子群。
If you take groups of order 12, it's not necessarily true, so let's just make that remark so that we start to appreciate this before we prove it: Note, if d divides the order |G| of G, there need not be a subgroup of order d.

103
00:25:05,399 --> 00:25:19,480
例如：若取 G 为 4 个字母上的交错群 A_4，其阶为 12，但它没有任何6 阶子群！
And an example: if you take G to be the alternating group on four letters, A_4, has order 12, but it has no subgroup of order 6!

104
00:25:28,931 --> 00:25:33,372
好，请注意 6 不是素数幂。
Okay, so notice that 6 is not a power of a prime.

105
00:25:33,372 --> 00:25:58,240
西罗定理告诉我们的是：必然存在一个 3 阶子群 H（西罗 3-子群），以及一个 4 阶子群 H'（西罗 2-子群）。这些是由西罗定理保证必然存在的。但 6 是两个素数的乘积 pq，西罗定理对它未作断言。
What the Sylow theorems tell us is that there exists an H of order 3 (a Sylow 3-subgroup), and there would be an H' of order 4 (a Sylow 2-subgroup). Those things are forced by the Sylow theorem. But this is pq, Sylow theorem says nothing about that.

106
00:25:58,240 --> 00:26:10,788
所以在群论中这有时被称为“局部定理”：所谓局部，是指它局限于单个素数，你只聚焦于单一素数。
So sometimes this is called a local theorem in group theory: local because it's localized at one prime, you only focus in on one prime.

107
00:26:10,788 --> 00:26:22,293
好，我们开始证明。该定理已知有非常多的证明方法——我想现在至少已有二三十种证明被发现。
Okay, let's start the proof. There are many, many proofs known, many many proofs—I think there now must be 20 or 30 proofs of this theorem that have been discovered.

108
00:26:22,293 --> 00:26:26,614
我非常喜欢阿廷（Artin）教材中的证明，我将采用他的方法，以后或许也会给出其他证明。
And I like the one in Artin very much, I'm going to imitate it, I'll probably try to give you some others later.

109
00:26:26,614 --> 00:26:54,585
阿廷的证明是基于以下事实：若取 G 的阶 |G| = N，并计算二项式系数 binom(N, p^m)——N 就是这个数，选 p^m，抱歉，我老把记号搞混——binom(N, p^m) 与p 互素！
So Artin is basing it on the following fact: that if you take the order of G, and you take the binomial coefficient N choose p^m— N is this number, p^m, sorry, p^m, I keep using my notation wrong—binom(N, p^m) is prime to p!

110
00:26:54,585 --> 00:26:59,062
这就是我们将从群论外部借用的事实。为什么呢？
That's the fact we're going to use from outside of group theory. So why is that?

111
00:26:59,062 --> 00:27:23,000
写出这个二项式系数：它等于 N(N - 1)(N - 2) ... (N - p^m + 1) 除以 [p^m (p^m - 1) ... 1]。
Well, write down this binomial coefficient: it looks like this: N(N - 1) (N - 2) ... (N - p^m + 1) / [p^m (p^m - 1) ... 1].

112
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:37,051
好，若观察这个式子，我们将会看到：整除分子的 p 的幂次与整除分母的 p 的幂次是完全相同的！
Okay, if you take a look at this term, now we're just going to see: the power of p dividing the numerator and the power of p dividing the denominator are the same!

113
00:27:37,051 --> 00:27:49,600
这就是我们证明……这已知是一个整数，我们证明它与 p 互素的途径是计算整除分子的 p 幂次与整除分母的 p 幂次，并证明两者相等。
That's how we're going to... This happens to be an integer, and the way we're going to prove it's prime to p is we're going to calculate the power of p dividing the numerator, the power of p dividing the denominator, and we'll show they're the same.

114
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:16,262
这是处理分数整除性的一种漂亮方法，基于算术基本定理（素因数分解唯一性）。整除 N 的最高 p 幂次就是 p^m，所以我们在这里分子分母具有相同的 p 幂次。
So that's a nice thing you can do about fractions, it's based on uniqueness of prime factorization. Well, the power of p dividing N is p^m, so we have the same power of p here.

115
00:28:16,262 --> 00:28:23,760
整除 N - 1 的 p 幂次是多少？零！必然是零，因为 N 能被 p 整除，而 p >= 2。
What's the power of p dividing N - 1? Zero! Has to be zero, because N is divisible by p, and p >= 2.

116
00:28:23,760 --> 00:28:31,128
这恰好等于整除分母项 p^m - 1 的 p 幂次。那整除 N - 2 的 p 幂次呢？这取决于情况：p 可能是 2 对吧？
That's exactly the power of p dividing this term. Now what's the power of p dividing N - 2? Well, that depends: p might be 2, right?

117
00:28:31,128 --> 00:28:40,720
若 p = 2，有一阶 p 整除此项，也有一阶 p 整除分母项。
And if p is 2, you have one power of p dividing this, and you have one power of p dividing this.

118
00:28:40,720 --> 00:29:02,542
所以在一般情况下——顺便说一句这被称为 p-进赋值 v_p——整除 N - k 的 p 幂次等于整除 p^m - k 的 p 幂次。大家可以自行验证。
So in general—this is called by the way the p-adic valuation v_p—the power of p dividing N - k is equal to the power of p dividing p^m - k. And I'll let you check that out.

119
00:29:02,542 --> 00:29:18,783
顺便说一下，这些 k都严格小于 p^m，所以特别地，整除 k 的 p 幂次最多为 m- 1。
These k's by the way are all less than p^m, so in particular the power of p dividing k is less than or equal to m minus 1.

120
00:29:18,783 --> 00:29:28,359
因此无论该幂次是多少，它都由整除 k 的 p 幂次决定，且恰好与分母中的幂次完全相同。
So whatever this power is, it's easily calculated by the power of p dividing k, and that's exactly the same as the power here.

121
00:29:28,359 --> 00:29:35,836
所以在每一项中，整除分子的 p 幂次都与整除分母的相匹配，一直到最后这一项，它既不能被p 整除，分母这项也不能。
So in each term you get a matching of the powers of p dividing the terms, right down to here, where this is not divisible by p, neither is this.

122
00:29:35,836 --> 00:29:44,274
因此综合相加后，分子的 p 总幂次与分母的 p 总幂次完全相同，计算出这个组合数后，它不能被 p 整除！
And so when you add them up, the power of p in the numerator is the same as the power of p in the denominator, and when you calculate this number, it's not divisible by p!

123
00:29:44,274 --> 00:30:15,668
好，这就是证明的关键，因为我们将让群作用在具有该大小的集合上：令 G 作用在集合 S 上——这是个奇特的集合——即 G 的所有大小为 p^m 的子集构成的集合。
Okay, now that's the key to the proof, because what we do is we have the group act on a set which has this size: let G act on the set—this is a weird set S—of all subsets of G which have size p^m.

124
00:30:15,668 --> 00:30:23,886
我们正试图证明存在该阶的子群，但目前尚不知道；不过我们显然能找到该大小的子集，对吧？
We're trying to prove there's a subgroup of this order, but we don't know that; we can certainly find subsets of that size, right?

125
00:30:23,886 --> 00:30:41,026
因为该大小小于或等于 N，且该大小子集的总数就是这个二项式系数 binom(N, p^m)。所以我们知道 S 的元素个数与p 互素。
Because this size is less than or equal to N, and the number of subsets of that size is this binomial coefficient binom(N, p^m). So we know that the number of elements in S is prime to p.

126
00:30:41,026 --> 00:31:04,903
好，现在我们将通过该集合中某个元素的稳定子群来得到西罗子群：作为此作用下的稳定子群 G_s。
Okay, now we're going to get our Sylow subgroup as the stabilizer of something in that set: as a stabilizer G_s for this action.

127
00:31:04,903 --> 00:31:12,699
这是从集合作用中获取子群的一种有效方式：固定某个点的稳定子群必为子群，对吧？
And that's one way of getting subgroups out of actions on sets: anything that stabilizes a point is a subgroup, right?

128
00:31:12,699 --> 00:31:23,760
虽然被作用的对象并非子群，但我们将看到其中某个子集会被一个阶为 p^m 的群 H 所稳定。
So the things we're acting on are not subgroups, but we're going to see that one of these sets is stabilized by a group H of order p^ m.

129
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,012
好，为什么呢？
Okay, why?

130
00:31:25,012 --> 00:31:56,648
我们使用一贯的轨道分解方法将该作用分解为轨道，这表明 S 的元素个数等于第一条轨道的元素个数加上第二条轨道的元素个数，一直加到最后一条轨道的元素个数。
Well, we use our usual orbit method to break this action into orbits, which tells us that the number of elements in S is equal to the number of elements in the first orbit plus the number of elements in the second orbit, plus the number of elements in the k-th orbit.

131
00:31:56,648 --> 00:32:18,599
在每条轨道上群都是传递作用的：所以第一条轨道的大小为 |G| 除以 s_1 的稳定子群的阶；第二条轨道的大小为 |G| 除以s_2 的稳定子群的阶，依此类推。
And on each orbit the group acts transitively: so the first orbit has size |G| divided by the order of the stabilizer of s_1; and the second orbit has size |G| divided by the order of the stabilizer of s_2, down to |G| divided by the stabilizer of s_k.

132
00:32:18,599 --> 00:32:37,669
这就是我们处理集合上的群作用时的一般方法：对于有限集，我们将其分解为轨道，在每条轨道上群传递作用，因此轨道大小等于 |G| 除以稳定子群的阶，因为传递作用同构于在稳定子群陪集上的作用。
So that's what we've been doing in general for group actions on sets: it's a finite set, we break it into orbits, on each orbit the group acts transitively, so the size of the orbit is |G| modulo the stabilizer, because the transitive action is modeled on the action on cosets of the stabilizer.

133
00:32:37,669 --> 00:32:39,326
好，|S| 与 p 互素。
Okay, |S| is prime to p.

134
00:32:39,326 --> 00:32:50,100
如果这每一条轨道的大小都能被 p 整除，那绝不可能把它们相加后得到与 p 互素的数，对吧？
If every one of these orbits had size divisible by p, there's no way you could add them all up and get some number prime to p, correct?

135
00:32:50,100 --> 00:33:18,167
因此结论是至少存在一条轨道的大小与 p 互素：存在至少一条大小与 p 互素的轨道，对吧？
So the conclusion is that at least one orbit has size prime to p: there is at least one orbit of size prime to p, correct?

136
00:33:18,167 --> 00:33:41,982
好，我们不妨称其为 s_1 的轨道，重新编号设 |O(s_1)| 与 p 互素，或者记作 O(s)，其中 s 是这些s_i 之一。好，现在我们看这对稳定子群意味着什么：
Okay, let's call that the orbit of s_1, say |O(s_1)| is prime to p by reordering, or let's just call it O(s), where s is one of these s_i. Okay, now we see what that says about the stabilizer:

137
00:33:41,982 --> 00:34:14,440
由于 |O(s)| = |G| / |G_s| = (p^m * n) / |G_s|与 p 互素，因此 p 的该次幂 p^m 必须整除稳定子群的阶！
since |O(s)| = |G| / |G_s| = (p^m * n) / |G_s| is prime to p, we must have this power p^m dividing the order of the stabilizer!

138
00:34:14,925 --> 00:34:33,697
好，因为如果一个表示为整数除以整数的分数与 p 互素，那么整除分母的 p 幂次必须等于整除分子的 p 幂次——与二项式系数同样的论证。所以 p^m 必整除稳定子群的阶。
Okay, because if you have a number expressed as an integer over an integer and it's prime to p, the power of p dividing the denominator must equal the power of p dividing the numerator—same argument we did for the binomial coefficient. So p^m divides the order of the stabilizer.

139
00:34:33,697 --> 00:34:42,279
形势开始变得乐观了！如果我们能证明它不大于 p^m，我们就能得到西罗子群。
So this is beginning to look good! If we could just show that it wasn't any larger than p^m, then we'd have our Sylow subgroup.

140
00:34:42,279 --> 00:34:58,440
但我断言——这是关键之处——稳定子群的阶至多为 p^m。
But I claim—and this is the key thing—that the stabilizer has order <= p^m.

141
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:10,671
好，我们马上就会看到这一点。
Okay, we're going to see that in a second.

142
00:35:10,671 --> 00:35:23,398
顺便说一句——天哪，我甚至还没告诉大家 G 是如何作用在集合上的！我说了让它作用在集合上，但我没说它是怎么作用的！
I should have said by the way—oh my God, I didn't even tell you how G acted on the sets! I said let it act on the sets, but I didn't tell you how it acted!

143
00:35:23,398 --> 00:35:50,589
抱歉，我是要让它通过左平移作用在集合上，通过左平移：如果我有 G 的一个子集（我最好不叫它 H，我叫它 J ⊆ G），它被映为 gJ ⊆ G（左平移），该子集与原集合大小相同。
So, no, I wanted it to act on the sets by translation, sorry, by left translation: so if I have a subset of G, which I better not call H, I'll call it J in G, it goes to gJ in G by left translation, so this set has the same size as this set.

144
00:35:50,589 --> 00:36:12,695
（是的，您是在交替使用……交替使用记号，抱歉。这也意味着 |G_s|……我应该更有条理些，如果我是布尔巴基（Bourbaki），我肯定会固定一种记号，但我却混着用了。
(Yeah, just to be... you're using them interchangeably? Interchangeably, I'm sorry. This also means the order of G_s... I should be more systematic, and if I were Bourbaki I would have chosen one and used that one, but I'm using them interchangeably.

145
00:36:12,695 --> 00:36:23,147
提得很好，很好！我们复盘一下：群在集合上的作用类似于通过左平移作用在群的元素上，而非共轭；它将子集 J 映为子集 gJ。
Good point, good point! So let's go over it: the action on the set is like it acts on points of the group by left translation, not by conjugation; so it takes a set J to this set gJ.

146
00:36:23,147 --> 00:36:33,821
此前的论证并不依赖于该作用具体是什么，未涉及作用形式，只用到被作用集合的元素个数与 p 互素这一事实。
And so the rest of this argument didn't depend on what the action was, made no reference to the action, just used the fact that the number of things it's acting on is prime to p.

147
00:36:33,821 --> 00:36:45,200
因此必然存在某条大小与 p 互素的轨道；因而必然存在某个稳定子群被 p^m 整除。但现在利用具体作用，我断言G_s 的阶至多为 p^m。
Therefore there has to be some orbit of size prime to p; therefore there has to be some stabilizer divisible by p^m. But now I'm going to claim, using the action, that the order of G_s is less than or equal to p^m.

148
00:36:45,200 --> 00:37:13,982
事实上，我断言子集 J 是……抱歉，让我想想怎么表述——我每次讲到这里总容易卡壳。
In fact, I claim that the subset J is a union of... Sorry, let's see how I want to say this—I always get confused at this point.

149
00:37:13,982 --> 00:37:24,104
啊，对了，对的，是的：这个点 s 就是一个子集 J。
Ah, yes, yes, yes: this point s is a subset J.

150
00:37:24,104 --> 00:37:38,296
所以 s 对应于 G 中的某个子集 J，取该子集的稳定子群中的元素。
So s corresponds to some subset J in G, and I have an element of the stabilizer of that subset.

151
00:37:38,296 --> 00:37:47,149
我们来写：若 g ∈ G_s，则 gJ = J。
So let's write: if g is in G_s, then gJ = J.

152
00:37:47,149 --> 00:37:53,509
我是说，它……它必须是大小相同的集合，所以它等于 J，包含在 J 中。
I mean, it... it has to be a set of the same size, so it's equal to J, it's contained in J.

153
00:37:53,509 --> 00:38:18,880
接着我断言这蕴含了 J 是稳定子群 G_s 的若干个左陪集的并！
And then I claim that this implies that J is a union of left cosets of G_s.

154
00:38:19,302 --> 00:38:29,345
特别地，已知 J 的大小为 p^m，它是 |G_s| 的若干倍总和。
In particular, the size of J, which we know is p^m, is a sum of |G_s| a number of times.

155
00:38:29,345 --> 00:38:35,886
特别地，G_s 的阶必定小于或等于子集 J 的大小！
In particular, the order of G_s is less than or equal to the size of J!

156
00:38:35,886 --> 00:38:45,806
我断言如果元素在稳定子群中就有此性质，这迫使 J 是 G_s 的陪集的并。
I claim that if you have an element in the stabilizer, you have this, and that forces J to be a union of cosets for G_s.

157
00:38:45,806 --> 00:39:09,693
因为如果考虑 G_s在此的作用：G_s 的陪集中……若 J 包含某个元素，那么该元素所在的整个陪集都落在 J 中，对吧？
Because if you think of the action of G_s here: the cosets of G_s... If you have one element in J, then you have all the elements of that coset in J, right?

158
00:39:09,693 --> 00:39:25,919
看看我思路是否清晰……是的，若我在某个陪集中有一个元素，假设J 包含该陪集中的一个元素，那么整个陪集都在 J 中，因为 G_s 的左乘保持 J 不变。
Let's see if I've got it the right way... Yeah, if I have an element in one of these cosets, suppose I have an element in this coset in J, then I claim that I have all of that coset in J, because G_s stabilizes J by left multiplication.

159
00:39:25,919 --> 00:39:32,480
所以它留在该陪集中，且通过 G_s 的左平移可由陪集中任意元素得到该陪集的全部元素。
So I stay in that coset, and I can get anything in that coset from anything else in that coset by translation by G_s.

160
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:41,279
同样，若子集 J 包含另一个陪集中的元素，由 G_s 保持 J 的事实，通过 G_s 平移可得到该陪集的所有元素。
Likewise, if my subset J contains some element in another coset, then by the fact that G_s stabilizes J, I can get anything in that coset by translating by G_s.

161
00:39:41,279 --> 00:39:48,705
因此在 G_s 下保持不变的子集只能是这些左陪集的并。
And consequently the only subsets stable under G_s are a union of these left cosets.

162
00:39:48,705 --> 00:39:57,680
从而 J 的大小必大于等于 |G_s|，因为|G_s| 就是单个陪集的大小。证明第一部分就此完成！
And consequently the size of J has to be >= |G_s|, because the order of G_s is the size of one of the cosets. And that's the end of the proof!

163
00:39:57,680 --> 00:40:05,680
首先是 p^m 整除此阶；但另一方面，子集的稳定子群的阶至多为 p^m。
The first was that p^m divides this order; but on the other hand, the stabilizer of a subset has order less than or equal to p^m.

164
00:40:05,680 --> 00:40:17,374
事实上，你会发现一个子集的稳定子群的阶恰好为 p^m 当且仅当它是一个西罗 p-子群。这就完成了该部分的论证。
And in fact, you'll find that a subset has stabilizer of order exactly p^m if and only if it's a Sylow p-subgroup. And that's the end of the argument.

165
00:40:17,374 --> 00:40:47,674
（虽然证明并不需要这点，事实上 J 具有 p^m 阶稳定子群当且仅当 J 是西罗 p-子群 H 的一个陪集，此时稳定子群即为 H。）
(Although you don't need it, in fact J has stabilizer of order p^m if and only if J is a coset of a Sylow p-subgroup H, in which case the stabilizer is H.)

166
00:40:47,674 --> 00:41:05,997
所以具有此阶稳定子群的唯一子集——而我们必然存在一个稳定子群能被此数整除的子集——就是西罗 p-子群。这就证明了p^m 阶子群的存在性！
So the only subsets that have a stabilizer of this order—and we have to have one subset whose stabilizer is divisible by this—are the Sylow p-subgroups. And that's the proof of the existence of a subgroup of order p^m.

167
00:41:05,997 --> 00:41:28,919
这确实是一个相当复杂的论证，大家课后需要慢慢理顺：整除性论证表明必存在某个稳定子群被该数整除，但任何稳定子群的阶都小于或等于该数；因此必存在某个阶恰好等于该数的稳定子群，而它正好就是你的西罗 p-子群。
So again, this is a fairly complicated argument, you've got to go through it yourself slowly: a divisibility argument shows that you have to have some stabilizer divisible by this number, but any stabilizer has order less than or equal to that number; therefore there has to be some stabilizer of order equal to that number, and that happens to be your Sylow p-subgroup.

168
00:41:28,919 --> 00:42:23,354
好，这是该定理容易的部分。现在我们证明第二部分。好，这部分非常巧妙。设 H 是由 (1) 找到的西罗子群。这是第二部分：我们让群 G 传递作用在 H 的陪集空间 G/H 上，其大小为 n，与p 互素。
Okay, that's the easy part of the theorem. Now let's prove part two. All right, now this is quite cute. Suppose I take my Sylow subgroup H, which is the Sylow subgroup found by (1). This is part two: and I have the group G act transitively on the coset space of H, G/H, which has size n prime to p.

169
00:42:23,354 --> 00:42:43,594
所以在知道西罗 p-子群存在之前，我费了很大劲去构造群在一个大小与 p 互素的集合上的作用——即全体大小为 p^m 的子集；但现在我们在大小与p 互素的集合上拥有自然的传递作用！
So before I knew the existence of a Sylow p-subgroup, I had to work quite hard to find an action of the group on a set of size prime to p—on the set of all subsets of size p^m; but here I have a natural transitive action on a set of size prime to p!

170
00:42:43,594 --> 00:43:04,295
好，在此作用下S 中任意点 s 的稳定子群 G_s 是H 的共轭子群，对吧？
Okay, the stabilizers of any point s in S, G_s, are the conjugates of H, right?

171
00:43:04,295 --> 00:43:13,861
因为这是传递作用：H 是固定单位陪集 1H 的子群，其它陪集则被其共轭子群固定。
Because it's a transitive action: H is the subgroup that stabilizes the identity coset, the other cosets are stabilized by conjugates.

172
00:43:13,861 --> 00:43:41,738
所以 G_s 就是陪集 sH 的稳定子群，它就是共轭子群 s H s^{-1}。该陪集的稳定子群就是这个共轭子群，所以它也是一个西罗 p-子群；通过考察此作用中各点的稳定子群，
So G_s would be the stabilizer for the coset sH, and it would be the conjugate s H s^{-1}, the stabilizer of that coset would be this conjugate, so that's also a Sylow p- subgroup; and we get all the conjugates of Sylow

173
00:43:41,738 --> 00:44:10,080
我们能得到该西罗 p-子群的所有共轭子群。好，现在看为什么任何 p-群都包含在其中一个共轭子群中。设 K 为……好的，我停一下。我们将证明任何……顺便说一下，这类群被称为 p-群，即 p^a 阶群。
p-subgroups by taking the stabilizers of points in this action. Okay, now let's see why any p- group is contained in one of these. Let K... sure, I'll stop. So we're going to try to prove that any... By the way, these things are called p-groups, groups of order p^a.

174
00:44:10,080 --> 00:44:24,986
我们已经找到一个西罗子群；我断言其共轭子群是在左作用下此集合中其它点的稳定子群：稳定该陪集就会得到该共轭子群，且任何共轭子群都来自这样的稳定子群。
So we found one Sylow group; I claim that its conjugates are the stabilizers of other points in this set for the left action: if you want to stabilize this coset you get this conjugate, and any conjugate comes from such a stabilizer.

175
00:44:24,986 --> 00:44:53,945
现在我们取另一个 p-群，另一个 p-子群 K，让 K 通过限制 G 在 S 上的作用来作用于 S：即让 K 通过左平移作用在H 的陪集上——只需将 G-作用限制到 K，这很自然。
And now I'm going to start with another p-group, another p-subgroup K, and have K act by the restriction of the G-action on S: namely have K act on the cosets of H by left translation—just restrict the G-action to K, that makes sense.

176
00:44:53,945 --> 00:45:19,314
好，由于集合的大小与 p 互素，因此在 K 的作用下必然存在一条大小与 p 互素的轨道，不妨设为 sH 的轨道，其大小与p 互素！
Okay, again, since the size of the set is prime to p, there must be an orbit, say the orbit of sH, of size prime to p!

177
00:45:19,314 --> 00:45:32,882
因为如果所有轨道的大小都能被 p 整除，那么整个集合的大小也必能被 p 整除，但事实并非如此。所以必有一条轨道，比如这条轨道，其大小与 p 互素。
Because if all the orbits had size divisible by p, the entire set would have size divisible by p, but it doesn't. So there must be an orbit, say this orbit, of size prime to p.

178
00:45:32,882 --> 00:45:58,520
这意味着其稳定子群……轨道的阶与 p 互素，所以 |K| 除以该点在 K 中的稳定子群的阶与 p 互素。
Which means that its stabilizer... The size of the orbit is prime to p, so |K| divided by the order of the stabilizer is prime to p.

179
00:46:00,240 --> 00:46:08,493
但 K 的阶是 p 的幂！这意味着稳定子群的阶必须等于K 的阶！
The order of K is a power of p! So that means that the order of the stabilizer has to be equal to the order of K!

180
00:46:08,493 --> 00:46:17,680
因此必然存在一个被 K 固定的单元素轨道。
So there must be an orbit fixed by K.

181
00:46:21,304 --> 00:46:31,170
由于 |K| = p^a，该点在 K 中的稳定子群的阶必等于K。
Since |K| = p^a, we must have the order of the stabilizer of that point is equal to the order of K.

182
00:46:31,170 --> 00:46:46,693
该点在 K 中的稳定子群是什么？它就是群 K ∩ G_s，即 G 中稳定子群落在K 中的元素，对吧？
What is the stabilizer of this point in K? That's just the group K ∩ G_s, the elements in the stabilizer in G which lie in K, correct?

183
00:46:46,693 --> 00:46:53,999
而我们已知 G_s 是 H 的共轭子群。
G_s, as we saw, was a conjugate of H.

184
00:46:57,680 --> 00:47:01,241
所以该交集的阶必须等于 K 的阶！
So the order of this group has to be the order of K!

185
00:47:01,241 --> 00:47:10,193
而这能够发生的唯一可能就是 K包含在这个群中！
And the only way that that can happen is if K is contained in this group!

186
00:47:10,193 --> 00:47:20,224
若 K 不完全包含在其中，当你将其与该子群求交时，所得子群必严格小于 K。但该交集的阶等于 K 的阶。
If K isn't totally contained in this group, when you intersect it with this subgroup you're going to get something strictly smaller than K. But the order of this intersection is the order of K.

187
00:47:20,224 --> 00:47:36,280
这表明我们最初选取的 p-群必包含在西罗 p-子群的某个共轭子群中；特别地，若我们一开始取的是西罗 p-子群，它就必然与之共轭！这是一种非常间接的证明。
That shows that the p-group we started with had to be contained in some conjugate of our Sylow p-subgroup; and in particular, that if we started with a Sylow p-subgroup, it was actually conjugate! Now this is very indirect.

188
00:47:36,280 --> 00:47:54,466
我们看看为何它如此间接：我们不知道 H 的哪一个共轭子群包含 K，因为我们不知道这里哪条轨道的大小与 p 互素；我们只知道必定存在一条，且无法通过该方法具体构造出来—
Let's see why it's so indirect: we don't know which conjugate of H contains K, because we don't know which orbit here has size prime to p; we just know there has to be one of them, and you can't actually find it by this method—

189
00:47:54,466 --> 00:48:09,451
—这纯粹是一个存在性证明。这是西罗定理的局限之一：它们并不是构造性的。最后，让我尝试证明 (3)——时间可能不太够，但我会在周三再回顾一下。
it's just an existence proof. That's one of the limitations of the Sylow theorems: they're not constructive. Finally, let me try to do (3)—we may not have enough time, but I'll start this again on Wednesday.

190
00:48:09,451 --> 00:48:22,123
仔细体会这些证明：它们是极其绝妙的计数论证，绝不会有人要求大家坐在那里独立把它们当作课后作业做出来。(3)：好，
Take a look through these proofs: they're exceedingly clever counting arguments, no one would suggest that one should just sit down and do these for homework! (3):

191
00:48:22,123 --> 00:48:51,265
我想我们现在能推导出来：西罗子群的数目，我们称为 ell 的西罗子群数目，我断言等于 |G| 除以某个西罗子群（西罗 p-子群）的正规化子的阶。
Okay, I think we can find it now: the number of Sylow subgroups, the number of Sylow subgroups which we called ell, is, I claim, |G| divided by the order of the normalizer of a Sylow subgroup, of a Sylow p-subgroup.

192
00:48:51,265 --> 00:49:24,304
因为 G 通过共轭传递作用在全体西罗p-子群构成的集合上（这是第二部分），且在共轭作用下 H 的稳定子群就是 H 的正规化子。
Because G acts transitively on the set of Sylow p-subgroups by conjugation (that's part two), and the stabilizer of H is what we called the normalizer of H under the conjugacy action.

193
00:49:24,304 --> 00:49:35,154
因此西罗子群的数目等于G 的阶除以该作用中某个点的稳定子群（即正规化子）。无论正规化子具体为何，它都包含 H，对吧？
So the number of Sylows is the order of G divided by the stabilizer of a point in that action, that's the normalizer. Whatever the normalizer is, it contains H, right?

194
00:49:35,154 --> 00:49:45,467
因此正规化子的阶能被 p^m 整除，因此西罗子群的数目必整除剩余的部分 n。
So the order of the normalizer is divisible by p^m, and therefore the number of them divides what's left, n.

195
00:49:45,467 --> 00:49:53,319
这是第一部分：该数目整除n。
That's the first part: that the number divides n.

196
00:49:54,399 --> 00:50:20,936
因为 H 包含在 N_G(H) 中，N_G(H) 的阶能被 p^m 整除，所以 ell 整除剩余的部分 n——也就是 |G| / p^m。
Since H is contained in N_G(H), N_G(H) has order divisible by p^m, so ell divides what's left, which is n— which is |G| / p^m.

197
00:50:20,936 --> 00:50:26,560
这就是整除性断言。现在我们需要证明同余断言。
That's the divisibility statement. Now we have to prove the congruence statement.

198
00:50:26,560 --> 00:50:34,000
这同样将是一个建立群轨道的问题。
Again, this is going to be one of these setting up an orbit problem.

199
00:50:34,000 --> 00:51:08,886
现在考虑该作用：我们已知全群通过共轭传递作用；将作用在全体西罗子群上的共轭作用限制在子群 H 自身。于是我们有一个包含 ell 个西罗子群的集合，现在让子群 H 通过共轭作用其上。
Now consider the action: we know the group acts transitively by conjugation; restrict the action of conjugation on the Sylows to the subgroup H itself. So we have a set of ell Sylows, and now we just let the subgroup H act by conjugation.

200
00:51:08,886 --> 00:51:34,564
我断言存在一个仅含 1 个元素的轨道——仅含 1 个元素——而所有其它轨道的元素个数均为 p^a（其中 a >= 1）。
I claim there's an orbit with 1 element—has 1 element—and all other orbits have p^a elements with a >= 1.

201
00:51:34,564 --> 00:51:36,280
这就是断言！
That's the claim!

202
00:51:36,280 --> 00:51:54,187
如果是这样，那么集合中总数 ell 就模 p 同余于 1，因为它是 1 加上 p 的倍数。好，为什么所有其它轨道都包含p^a 个元素呢？
If that's the case, then the total number in the set, ell, is congruent to 1 mod p, because it's 1 plus p times other things. Okay, why do all other orbits have p^a elements?

203
00:51:54,187 --> 00:52:11,040
因为这是 H 的轨道，H 的阶是 p^m，所以任何轨道的阶都整除 |H|，因此必须是 p 的某次幂。你只需证明它不可能为1！
Well, they have some power of p elements because it's an orbit of H, which has order p^m; and so the size of any orbit divides |H|, so it has to be some power of p. You just have to show it can't be 1!

204
00:52:16,580 --> 00:52:42,737
假设存在另一个在 H 的共轭下保持不变的西罗 p-子群。若 H' 落在大小为1 的轨道中，那么 H 正规化 H'，对吧？
So suppose there was another Sylow p-subgroup that was stable under conjugation by H. If H' were in an orbit of size 1, then H normalizes H', right?

205
00:52:42,737 --> 00:52:56,840
这表明在 H 的共轭下 H' 稳定，所以 H 正规化 H'。于是 H 与 H' 都是正规化子 N_G(H') 的子群。
That just says that under conjugation by H, H' is stable, so H normalizes H'. So H and H' are two subgroups of the normalizer N_G(H').

206
00:52:56,840 --> 00:53:16,386
这步太绝妙了，准备好了吗？请看：N_G(H') 是 G 的子群，其阶为 p^m * n'，其中包含同样的素数幂 p^m。
Now this is a killer, are you ready? Watch this: N_G(H') is a subgroup of G, so its order is p^m * n' for some n'.

207
00:53:16,563 --> 00:53:29,550
特别地，整除其阶的 p 的最高次幂与整除 G 阶的 p 幂次完全相同，因为它包含了 H。因此这两个群都是 N_G(H') 的西罗 p-子群，对吧？
In particular, this power of p is the same power of p that divided the order of G; it has to be there because it contains H. Therefore these two things are Sylow p-subgroups of N_G(H'), correct?

208
00:53:29,550 --> 00:53:39,376
现在我们把 G 抛在一边：它们俩都是 N_G(H') 的西罗p-子群！
We forget about G now: they're now both Sylow p-subgroups of this group!

209
00:53:39,376 --> 00:53:43,378
而西罗定理适用于任何有限群。
And we can apply the Sylow theorems to any finite group.

210
00:53:43,378 --> 00:53:59,302
所以现在我们将其应用于该子群，由已经证过的第 (2)部分可知，它们在该群中必共轭——即在 H' 的正规化子中互为共轭！但在 H' 的正规化子中，与 H' 共轭的唯一子群只有 H' 自身！
So now we apply them to this group, and part (2), which we've proved already, says that they're conjugate in that group—so conjugate in the normalizer of H'! But in the normalizer of H', the only thing conjugate to H' is H' itself!

211
00:53:59,302 --> 00:54:07,639
若看该群内部对 H' 的共轭作用，它根本不移动H'。
If you look at the action of conjugation on H' inside of this group, it doesn't move it at all.

212
00:54:07,639 --> 00:54:14,604
因此 H' 必然等于 H！这证明了大小为 1 的轨道恰好只有一条。
So H' is equal to H! And that shows there's only one orbit of size 1.

213
00:54:14,604 --> 00:54:26,639
这真是一个绝妙而震撼的论证，因为你脱离了全群G，转而将西罗定理已证的第 (1)、(2) 部分直接应用于子群 N_G(H')！
It's a totally cool killer argument, because you leave the group G, and you just apply the Sylow theorems to a subgroup—the parts that you've proved, (1) and (2)!

214
00:54:26,639 --> 00:54:40,754
所以请仔细品味这个惊艳的论证。周三我们将回来稍微回顾一下，然后我将通过实例向大家展示如何对 pq 阶群进行分类。
So take a look at this amazing argument. We'll come back and review it a little Wednesday, and then I'm going to give you some examples to show you how you classify groups of order pq.
